    "notes": "Wikidata Q109968 identifies the plaza. Its central monument Q86518088 matches the named PMTiles feature and seven central components. The mapped pedestal edge sets the axis. The Genius faces the southern approach as shown by the front photograph and Smithsonian record. The monument proportions combine seven mapped components with the exterior photographs. The statue height follows the roughly 76-foot total, while the mapped procedural envelope is 25 m. Sculpture faces, drapery and reliefs are medium-fi reconstructions. The fountains use fixed water levels and static jet arcs. Paving follows the standard terrain and retains native street, footway and planting data. Physical-device timings are unmeasured."
  },
